    "text": {
     "en": "The poem describes children gathering in a playground with a stick and a small gilli, playing happily.\nThey count one, two, three, swing and hit, and say with friends they never quit.\nWith every swing they feel free, and the gilli flies high under the bright blue sky.\nThey laugh and play under the golden rays of the sun.\nThe poem shows that playing outdoors with friends brings joy and a feeling of freedom.\n(additional, not in the textbook) Traditional games like gilli danda cost little and keep us active."
    }
